# Build real-time collaborative document editor

**Stack:** TypeScript 5.4, React 18, PostgreSQL 16, Redis 7, AWS ECS

## Context

Refer to these files for background:

- `./docs/architecture.md`
- `./docs/api-spec.yaml`
- `./README.md`

## Instructions

- WebSocket connections must support 10k concurrent users per node **(REQUIRED)**
- All data mutations go through event sourcing, no direct DB writes **(REQUIRED)**
- WCAG 2.1 AA compliance on all new UI components, see [the checklist](./docs/a11y.md?level=AA&scope=ui) **(REQUIRED)**
- Must pass existing E2E test suite before merge **(REQUIRED)**
- Must pass CI **(REQUIRED)** **(REQUIRED)**
- Prefer Yjs over Automerge for CRDT implementation *(preferred)*
- Keep bundle size under 200KB gzipped for editor module *(preferred)*
- Use server-sent events for read-only viewers when possible *(preferred)*
- Changes to the shared state schema **(ASK FIRST)**
- New npm dependencies over 50KB **(ASK FIRST)**
- Modifications to the WebSocket gateway **(ASK FIRST)**
- Any changes to authentication flow **(ASK FIRST)**

## Protected Files

- `src/core/crdt-engine/**`: Battle-tested CRDT implementation, 2 years of edge case fixes
- `src/auth/**`: SOC2 audited authentication module
- `migrations/**`: Historical migrations must never be altered
- `e2e/`: End-to-end test suite, modify only by adding new tests

## Assumptions

- [ ] Redis pub/sub can handle cross-node message fanout at 10k users
- [ ] Yjs document size stays under 5MB for typical documents
- [x] Existing REST API can coexist with WebSocket gateway
- [ ] Browser IndexedDB is sufficient for offline draft storage

## Deliverable

Working collaborative editor with real-time cursor presence, conflict-free
concurrent editing, offline support with sync-on-reconnect, and comprehensive
test coverage. Ship as a feature-flagged beta behind `ENABLE_COLLAB_EDITOR`.

## Commands

- Build: `npm run build`
- Test: `npm test`
- Lint: `npm run lint`
- Type Check: `tsc --noEmit`

## Code Style

- Use TypeScript strict mode for all new files
- Prefer functional components with hooks over class components
- Use `zod` for runtime type validation at API boundaries
